---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 1,
        "name": "Home",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 2,
        "name": "Services",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/services"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 3,
        "name": "Conversational Analytics",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/conversational-analytics"
      }
    ]
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Conversational Analytics | Alluvium"
  description="Conversational analytics for Power BI: ask plain-language questions and get answers grounded in the reports you already trust."
  canonicalPath="/conversational-analytics"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="service-fold">
<article>
<header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><a href="/services">Services</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span>Conversational Analytics</span></nav>

<h1 class="page-title">Conversational Analytics</h1>
<p class="lede">Ask questions in plain language and get answers from the Power BI reports your team already trusts.</p>
</div></header>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap">
<h2>Answers that match your reporting</h2>
<p>People already ask questions by email and in the hallway. When answers come from different spreadsheets, they drift from what leadership just reviewed. Your Power BI reports already hold the agreed definitions for revenue, margin, inventory, and cash.</p>
<p>Questions go to those reports, so answers stay consistent with what the report shows.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="band band-alt"><div class="wrap">
<h2>Questions go to trusted reports</h2>
<p>Loose spreadsheets stay out of it. Questions go to the reports leadership already uses.</p>
<figure class="diagram"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 640 240" role="img" aria-label="A question mark points at one report. Loose sheets sit off to the side.">
<circle cx="70" cy="78" r="28" fill="none" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="6"/>
<path d="M58 70c0-12 24-14 24 2 0 10-12 10-12 20" fill="none" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
<circle cx="70" cy="112" r="4" fill="#397fb0"/>
<line x1="110" y1="96" x2="230" y2="120" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="4"/>
<rect x="236" y="36" width="150" height="176" rx="4" fill="#e7f1f8" stroke="#1c1c1c" stroke-width="2.5"/>
<rect x="256" y="58" width="110" height="16" fill="#397fb0"/>
<rect x="256" y="90" width="24" height="78" fill="#1c1c1c"/>
<rect x="292" y="114" width="24" height="54" fill="#397fb0"/>
<rect x="328" y="102" width="24" height="66" fill="#397fb0" opacity="0.75"/>
<rect x="460" y="40" width="130" height="18" rx="2" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#dcdcdc"/>
<rect x="478" y="70" width="130" height="18" rx="2" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#dcdcdc"/>
<rect x="448" y="100" width="130" height="18" rx="2" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#dcdcdc"/>
<rect x="492" y="130" width="120" height="18" rx="2" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="#dcdcdc"/>
</svg></figure>
</div></section>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap">
<h2>What has to be true first</h2>
<p>The report must already be trusted, with agreed definitions, timely refresh, correct access, and an internal owner who can update definitions.</p>
<p>If that isn't in place yet, start there. A <a href="/analytics-ai-strategy-roadmap">roadmap</a>, a <a href="/power-bi-dashboard-optimization-ai-insights">cleanup of the report you have</a>, or <a href="/power-bi-training">training on that report</a> may need to come first.</p>
<h2>Where the answer comes from</h2>
<p>You or your analysts ask in plain language. Answers are calculated from your existing Power BI reports, using the same definitions.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="band related-links" aria-labelledby="related-services">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="related-services">Related Power BI Services</h2>
    <ul><li><a href="/power-bi-model-health">Power BI model health</a></li>
<li><a href="/power-bi-dashboard-optimization-ai-insights">Dashboard optimization</a></li>
<li><a href="/analytics-ai-strategy-roadmap">Analytics strategy roadmap</a></li></ul>
    <h2>Related Power BI Insights</h2>
    <ul><li><a href="/blog/conversational-analytics-needs-a-trusted-model">Conversational analytics needs a trusted model</a></li>
<li><a href="/blog/ask-the-model-dont-screenshot">Ask the model, do not screenshot</a></li>
<li><a href="/blog/semantic-model-is-the-product">The semantic model is the product</a></li></ul>
  </div>
</section><section class="band band-cta" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="cta-heading">Let's put your reports to work</h2>
    <p class="lede">Tell us about your reporting. We'll tell you whether it's ready for plain-language questions, and what to do first if not.</p>
    <p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a></p>
  </div>
</section></article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
